@startuml Amdox-ERP-Deployment
title Amdox ERP — Deployment Diagram (as-built on AWS)
skinparam shadowing false

' What this shows: where each piece physically runs in production.
' Everything lives inside ONE AWS EC2 instance running k3s (lightweight
' Kubernetes). The browser reaches it over HTTPS via the Traefik ingress.

node "User Device" {
  artifact "Browser\n(React SPA)" as browser
}

cloud "Internet" as net

node "AWS EC2  (Ubuntu 22.04)\nElastic IP 13.127.204.51" as ec2 {

  node "k3s  (single-node Kubernetes)" {

    component "Traefik Ingress\n+ cert-manager (Let's Encrypt TLS)" as ingress

    node "frontend  x2\n(nginx + Vite build)" as fe
    node "backend  x2\n(Node 22 + Express + BullMQ workers)" as be
    node "ml-service  x1\n(FastAPI + LSTM + Prophet)" as ml
    database "postgres-0\n(PostgreSQL 17, PVC)" as pg
    queue "redis\n(Redis 7)" as redis

    component "HPA\n(autoscale >70% CPU)" as hpa
    component "pg_dump CronJob\n(backup)" as backup
  }
}

browser --> net : HTTPS
net --> ingress : :443
ingress --> fe : /
ingress --> be : /api
be --> pg : Prisma (5432)
be --> redis : sessions + BullMQ (6379)
be --> ml : HTTP (8000)
hpa ..> be : scales
backup ..> pg : every 15 min

note right of ec2
  Single-box deploy via k8s/deploy-k3s.sh.
  Images built on the node and imported
  into k3s (no external registry).
  Not used (spec-optional): EKS, RDS,
  ElastiCache, S3, SES, Keycloak.
end note
@enduml
